card-image: img/kpd_car.jpg
frequency: 100
tags: party_affairs

= Campaigning

Whether or not we are in an electoral campaign, the party is always trying to broaden its voter base. Who should we focus our campaign efforts on?

- @workers: The urban working class, our traditional support base.
- @new_middle: The "new middle class" of government employees and white-collar workers.
- @old_middle: The "old middle class" of small independent businessmen and artisans, the petty bourgeoisie.
- @rural: Rural workers and small farmers, to reconcil town and country.
- @unemployed: The unemployed. [? if unemployed_kpd >=40: They are currently our strongest support base. ?]
- @catholics: Catholics, who typically support the Center Party.
- @root: We either don't want to or cannot campaign right now.
- @easy_discard

@workers
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: workers_kpd += 3*(1-dissent); workers_kpd -= 2 if unemployed >= 15; workers_kpd -= 2 if unemployed >= 25; workers_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if workers_kpd > workers_spd; resources -= 1; workers_kpd += 3*(1-dissent) if nationalization_progress >= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the workers. [? if unemployed >= 15: The high levels of unemployment make our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if workers_kpd < workers_spd : The SPD competes for our votes as they're the dominant left wing party. ?] [? if workers_kpd > workers_spd : As the more popular socialist party among workers, they have naturally began favoring us over the SPD. ?] 

@new_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: new_middle_kpd += 4*(1-dissent); new_middle_kpd -= 4 if socialism <= 49; resources -= 1;

We have increased our campaigning among the new middle class. [? if socialism <= 49: The popular antipathy towards socialism among this group makes our campaign more difficult. ?] [? if peoples_party > 0: As a people's party, we have an easier time increasing support among the middle class than before. ?]

@old_middle
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: old_middle_kpd += 5*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; old_middle_kpd -= 3 if nationalism >= 51; old_middle_kpd +=3 if socialism >=50

We have increased our campaigning among the old middle class. [? if nationalism >= 51 and peoples_party == 0: The reactionary nature of the petty bourgeois remain, in part due to our lack of campaigning. ?] [? if socialism >= 50: While technically against their class interest, the some in petty bourgeoisie have become socialists. If Engels could do it, so can they. ?]

@rural
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: rural_kpd += 5*(1-dissent); rural_kpd -= 4 if rural_connection <3; resources -=1

We have increased our campaigning among farmers. [? if rural_connection <3: We have not historically campaigned much among the farmers, and they do not trust us. ?] [? if rural_connection >= 3 : Our grassroot connection with the rural population had made campaigning easier. ?]

@unemployed
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
on-arrival: unemployed_kpd += 4*(1-dissent); resources -= 1; unemployed_kpd += 2 if welfare < 0; unemployed_nsdap += 2 if welfare < 0 ; unemployed_kpd -= 3*(1-dissent) if welfare >= 2;

We have increased our campaigning among the unemployed. [? if welfare < 0: The welfare cuts and resultant poverty by the SPD and bourgeois parties have radicalized the unemployed, perhaps in the wrong direction for some... ?][? if wtb_adopted = 1 : Adopting the WTB plan gives us a new rallying point around which to attract support from the unemployed. ?]

@catholics
subtitle: -1 resources
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough resources.
view-if: peoples_party == 1
on-arrival: catholics_spd += 6*(1-dissent); resources -= 1

We have increased our campaigning among Catholics.
